# Copy to `web/.env` and edit for this machine. That file is git-ignored; this one is the template.
#
# Everything here becomes an environment variable for the backend. A value already present in
# your shell wins, so `.env` sets defaults rather than forcing anything.

# --- Where the student model lives -------------------------------------------------------------
# The student route needs an OpenAI-compatible endpoint — any server that answers
# `/v1/models` and `/v1/chat/completions`. The `/v1` is part of the URL: the harness appends
# `/chat/completions` to what you write here rather than replacing a path, so a URL without it
# gets a 404.      (The backend also normalises this if you forget.)
#
# The recorded runs served Qwen3-4B on the training box behind Tailscale:
#   CHTD_STUDENT_URL=http://100.84.151.62:8003/v1
#   CHTD_STUDENT_MODEL_ID=qwen3-4b-instruct-2507
#
# A local server works the same way:
#   CHTD_STUDENT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
#
# Leave both commented out to keep the default (127.0.0.1:8000/v1), which will simply read as
# "not ready" until something answers there.

# --- The teacher ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A hosted API, so it needs a credential and nothing else, and it needs no GPU. The key is read
# from AGNES_SECRET_TEACHER_DEFAULT, or the file named by CHTD_LIVE_KEY_FILE.
#   CHTD_LIVE_KEY_FILE=E:\Coding\chtd\data\chtd-round-20261011\teacher.key
